// The Dream, Beta 1.0: story logic (Yarn Spinner). The acted scenes are films (story/SCRIPT.md); this decides which
// film plays, asks the choices in the game's UI, keeps the story variables, and holds the phone texts.
//   <<film id>>          play a rendered film and wait for it (Films/<id>.mp4)
//   <<money n "why">>    add to the bankroll
//   <<stake n>>          Slick lends n; half your profits go back until it's repaid
// Line tags: #card heads the next choice card, #hint explains the next option (in order), #text is a phone text from
// the speaker; any other line is a card on black.

title: Variables
---
// Variables the game sets before each run (game state, not saved here): $bankroll, $peak, $chapter (0 prologue,
// 1 Chapter 1), $room_title, and after an event $event, $won, $bust, $mistake.
<<declare $bankroll = 0>>
<<declare $peak = 0>>
<<declare $chapter = 0>>
<<declare $room_title = false>>
<<declare $event = "">>
<<declare $won = false>>
<<declare $bust = false>>
<<declare $mistake = false>>
// Story variables (saved with the career): the job, and what has already been seen.
<<declare $job = "">>
<<declare $david_seen = false>>
<<declare $lesson_seen = false>>
<<declare $needle_seen = false>>
<<declare $classic_seen = false>>
<<declare $classic_lose_seen = false>>
===

title: Decision
---
// Monday morning after the Biscayne Championship. The old game's p_after choice (dream/story.js, Story.cs).
<<film p_after>>
Monday, 9:06 AM · Floor 34 #card
Decision time. #card
Whatever you pick, Lou finds out today. #card
Slick backs you with $5,000. Play every day. #hint
$2,000 saved. A paycheck every Friday. Biscayne on weekends. #hint
-> Quit. Today.
    <<set $job to "quit">>
    <<money 5000 "Quit the 9-to-5. Slick's backing">>
    <<film p_quit>>
-> Keep the job. Grind nights.
    <<set $job to "nights">>
    <<money 2000 "Kept the day job. Savings">>
    <<film p_keep>>
<<film c1>>
===
